  <tei:text>
    <tei:body>
      <tei:div corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:prayer:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen">
        <tei:p><tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/1"/>We have acted wickedly and have transgressed;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/2"/>we have therefore not been delivered.
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/3"/>Grant that our hearts [be inspired to]
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/4"/>abandon the path of wickedness,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/5"/>and hasten our deliverance;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/6"/>as is written by the hand of Your prophet,
<tei:milestone unit="verse" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:isaiah/55/7"/>
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/7"/>“Let the wicked man abandon his ways,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/8"/>and the man of iniquity his thoughts;
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/9"/>and let him return unto Adonoy,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/10"/>and He will have compassion on him,
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/11"/>and unto our God
<tei:milestone unit="phrase" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:metsudah:hirshanu_ufashanu_lakhen/12"/>for He pardons abundantly.”
<tei:milestone unit="phrase"/>
<tei:milestone unit="verse"/></tei:p>
      </tei:div>
    </tei:body>
  </tei:text>
